Foster’s team is now investigating whether specific habits, such as reduced screen use before bedtime or consistent sleep schedules, can reliably increase time spent in this important deep sleep stage. She hopes that if such habits prove effective, simple, low-cost recommendations could be developed to help people improve memory and cognitive health without requiring medication, particularly benefiting older adults who often experience reduced deep sleep as they age.

【設問】
What is Foster’s team currently investigating?', NULL, '["Whether certain habits can increase time spent in deep sleep.","Whether people should stop using wearable devices entirely.","How to reduce the total amount of sleep people need.","Whether memory tests are affected by room temperature."]', 0, '["第4段落「特定の習慣が深い睡眠を増やせるか調査中」。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題・サイエンス時事編）', 913);
INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('tgweb_english', '長文問題', '睡眠の質と脳の健康', 'Sleep researchers have long known that insufficient sleep affects memory and concentration, but recent studies have focused more closely on how sleep quality, not just duration, influences long-term brain health. Poor-quality sleep, characterized by frequent interruptions or reduced time in deep sleep stages, has been linked to increased risk of several cognitive and metabolic problems, even when total sleep time appears normal.

Dr. Naomi Foster has led a long-term study tracking sleep patterns in over 3,000 participants using wearable devices that monitor brain activity throughout the night. Her research aims to identify which specific sleep stages are most important for memory consolidation, the process by which the brain stores new information as long-term memories. When Foster’s study began in 2014, researchers had limited ability to monitor sleep stages outside of laboratory settings. Advances in wearable technology have since made large-scale, real-world sleep monitoring possible.

In 2021, a member of Foster’s team, Marcus Webb, identified a strong correlation between time spent in a specific deep sleep stage and performance on memory tests conducted the following day. Participants who spent more time in this stage consistently outperformed others on tasks requiring recall of newly learned information, regardless of their total sleep duration. This finding suggested that sleep quality, particularly time spent in deep sleep, may matter more than sleep length alone.

Foster’s team is now investigating whether specific habits, such as reduced screen use before bedtime or consistent sleep schedules, can reliably increase time spent in this important deep sleep stage. She hopes that if such habits prove effective, simple, low-cost recommendations could be developed to help people improve memory and cognitive health without requiring medication, particularly benefiting older adults who often experience reduced deep sleep as they age.

【設問】
Which of the following statements is true?', NULL, '["Foster’s study has tracked sleep patterns in more than 3,000 participants.","Marcus Webb found that total sleep duration matters more than sleep quality.","Wearable sleep-monitoring technology was widely available before 2014.","Foster’s research is primarily focused on children’s sleep patterns."]', 0, '["第2段落に一致。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題・サイエンス時事編）', 913);
INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('tgweb_english', '長文問題', 'AI医療診断の実用化', 'Artificial intelligence has increasingly been applied to medical diagnosis, particularly in analyzing medical images such as X-rays and scans, where subtle patterns can be difficult for the human eye to detect consistently. While early AI diagnostic tools showed promise in controlled research settings, integrating them reliably into everyday clinical practice has proven more difficult than many developers initially expected.

Dr. Samuel Okafor, a radiologist, has worked for the past several years to evaluate how AI diagnostic tools perform when used alongside doctors in real hospital settings, rather than in isolated testing environments. His research compares diagnostic accuracy when doctors work with AI assistance versus when they work without it, across a range of medical conditions. When Okafor began this research in 2017, most AI diagnostic studies relied on small, carefully selected datasets. His team has since worked with larger, more diverse patient populations to test how well these tools generalize.

A significant finding came in 2022, when a data scientist on Okafor’s team, Lin Wei, discovered that AI tools trained primarily on data from one hospital often performed noticeably worse when used at hospitals with different patient populations or imaging equipment. This finding highlighted a problem known as poor generalization, where a tool that appears highly accurate in one setting fails to maintain that accuracy elsewhere, potentially leading to missed or incorrect diagnoses if not properly addressed.

In response, Okafor’s team has begun developing methods to train AI tools using data pooled from multiple hospitals with diverse equipment and patient demographics, aiming to improve consistency across different clinical settings. He stresses that AI should be viewed as a tool to support doctors’ judgment rather than replace it entirely. Okafor now hopes to establish clearer guidelines for testing AI diagnostic tools before they are approved for widespread hospital use, to ensure patient safety remains the top priority.

【設問】
What has proven more difficult than developers initially expected?', NULL, '["Building any AI tool that can analyze medical images at all.","Integrating AI diagnostic tools reliably into everyday clinical practice.","Convincing doctors that medical images exist.","Reducing the cost of medical imaging equipment."]', 1, '["第1段落「実際の臨床現場での統合は予想以上に困難」。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題・サイエンス時事編）', 914);
