Dr. Fatima Al-Rashid’s study compares', NULL, '["productivity, satisfaction, and career advancement across different work arrangements.","the cost of office rent in different cities.","the history of remote work technology.","employee preferences for different office furniture."]', 0, '["第2段落。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題・サイエンス時事編）', 916);
INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('tgweb_english', '長文問題', 'リモートワークとキャリア形成', 'Remote work became far more common following major shifts in workplace practices in the early 2020s, prompting researchers to examine its long-term effects on productivity and employee well-being more closely than before. While many workers reported enjoying greater flexibility, questions remained about whether remote work affected collaboration and long-term career development differently than traditional office settings.

Dr. Fatima Al-Rashid has led a multi-year study following employees at several companies that adopted flexible remote and hybrid work policies. Her research compares productivity, job satisfaction, and career advancement rates among employees working fully remotely, in hybrid arrangements, and fully in offices. When Al-Rashid began her study in 2020, most available data on remote work productivity came from short-term surveys rather than long-term tracking, making it difficult to draw firm conclusions.

In 2023, a data analyst on Al-Rashid’s team, Jonas Berg, identified that employees in hybrid arrangements, who split time between remote work and the office, reported the highest job satisfaction scores among the three groups, while showing productivity levels comparable to fully in-office employees. However, fully remote employees, despite reporting high satisfaction with flexibility, were promoted at notably lower rates than their hybrid or in-office peers over the study period.

Al-Rashid’s team is now investigating why fully remote employees experienced slower career advancement despite similar productivity levels, with early findings suggesting reduced visibility to managers and fewer informal networking opportunities may play a role. She hopes her research can help companies design remote and hybrid policies that preserve flexibility while ensuring all employees, regardless of work location, have equal opportunities for career growth and professional recognition.

【設問】
Jonas Berg’s finding showed that', NULL, '["fully remote employees were promoted at the highest rates.","hybrid employees reported the highest job satisfaction with productivity similar to in-office workers.","fully in-office employees reported the lowest job satisfaction.","remote work had no effect on employee satisfaction at all."]', 1, '["第3段落「ハイブリッド勤務者が最も満足度が高く生産性も同等」。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題・サイエンス時事編）', 916);
